# Tests for new work

Ship **behavior changes together with tests** in the same task. Do not treat tests as optional follow-up.

## When tests are required

- New user-visible behavior (canvas gestures, editing, drag/drop, keyboard shortcuts)
- New or changed store actions and domain logic
- Bug fixes (regression test that fails on old code, passes on the fix)

Skip tests only for pure refactors with no behavior change, or docs/comments-only edits.

## What to add (vira / Vitest)

| Layer | Location | Notes |
|-------|----------|--------|
| Domain | `src/domain/*.test.ts` next to module | Pure functions, no jsdom |
| Store | `src/store/*.test.ts` | `useDocument.getState().clearAll()` in `beforeEach` when needed |
| Gestures / DOM | `src/components/**/*.test.ts` | `// @vitest-environment jsdom`; follow `bindCanvasGestures*.test.ts` patterns |

Cover at least: **happy path**, one **edge case**, and **“does not happen when feature off”** when relevant (e.g. alt-drag vs normal drag).

## Before finishing

Run `npm test -- --run` and fix failures. New feature work is not done until tests pass.
